---
description: Fix one PokePilot run from its run id using the compact one-id debugger before expanding context.
globs:
alwaysApply: false
---

Follow @.claude/skills/pokefarm-run-fix/SKILL.md. The cheap/default path is:

1. `make -s debug RUN=<run-id>`.
2. Use its `packet`, measured `reproduction`, and bounded
   `source_matches`; do not repeat those MCP/artifact/search steps.
3. Only a real software defect earns a patch. Claim the linked issue when one
   exists.
4. Fix the shared owning invariant.
5. Rerun the same `make -s debug RUN=<run-id>`, then `make test-short`.
6. Push a `fix/*` branch, open the triage-keyed PR, and record the solver
   attempt.

Use full run-debug/recovery/artifact reads only when the prepared packet is
genuinely insufficient. Do not create throwaway repro tests for structured Red
failures; `pokedebug` already drives the deterministic executor verifier.
